For the majority of your needs, you could make your own cables.
Digikey, Mouser, Jameco sells the ribbon cable and connectors.  The
connectors are press-fit.....you don't need a connector press-
carefully align the two pieces of the connector along the cable, tap
with a hammer to initially seat it, then insert the connector length
wise along the vise and tighten.  Most types of ribbon cable can be
ordered in 5 foot (1.52m) lengths.
Just remember the length constraints on the cable.  IIRC scsi-1, 2 is
6m, scsi-2 fast, fast+wide is 3m, ultra scsi-3, is 1.5m.
Googling scsi cable requirements will provide the in formation you
will need to get the right cable (e.g. pitch, awg, shield/ground
plane, etc.

John


