I'm testing an XP1000.  I know that my console terminal (VT320) and
cable are working OK since they work on other machines.  This is plugged
in to the lower 9-pin serial plug (labeled "1") on the XP1000.  After
powering it on, I get a display of the PALcode for VMS and ALPHA, so it
looks like the machine can talk to the terminal.  Then, even after
several minutes, nothing.  (The other serial plug doesn't even show the 
PALcode message, so I'm assuming that "1" is the correct connector for 
the serial console.)

Any ideas?

Since there is a video card in the machine, maybe the console is set to 
GRAPHICS.  I tried typing "set console serial" and power cycling, but to 
no avail.

I like the VAX (an early ALPHA) concept: a physical switch on the
machine switches between serial and graphics console and indicates which 
is which by its position (though which position was which was not 
entirely consistent between models).

No more time today, but tomorrow I'll connect up a graphics monitor and 
see what happens.  Maybe that will work.  In the meantime, suggestions 
for trouble-shooting other potential problems which could prevent me 
from getting to the console are welcome.  :-|



