First, thanks to all who have provided me with hardware over the years.
I almost have enough to last me for the rest of my life, though when I
upgrade all machines in my main cluster to EV6 and faster disks, I might
need some additional spares.  I'm not yet sure what additional disks,
controllers, expansion boxes etc I need but am definitely happy to
collect in Europe any DS10, DS15 or XP1000 machines which are no longer
needed. (I actually don't have that much running at once, but if
something dies I want to be able to swap in a spare with minimal trouble
and have enough spares to last me as long as I live.) 

Second, my inventory is progressing and I plan to pass on some older
stuff I don't need (anymore).  I'll be contacting folks who have already
contacted me regarding this within the next few weeks. 

Third, I am (still) looking for (some) SCSI cables.  For now, I'm only
concerned with ten cable types (ignoring, say, the VAXstation 3100
cables).  There are four types of connector in these cables:

   A: really big 50-pin with wire-loop clamps (Centronics) (seen on VAX
      machines other than the VAXstation 3100 and large-case 
      first-generation ALPHAs)

   B: small 50-pin with squeeze clamps (seen on ALPHAs up through the 
      au Personal Workstation, i.e. before that the second-generation 
      EV4 boxes, the Top-Gun Blue boxes with EV45 and EV5 (AlphaStation)
      and the small-case workstations of the very first generation))

   C: 68-pin wider than B but of the same thickness (seen on the Top-Gun
      Blue boxes with EV45 and EV5 and everything after that)

   D: really small 68-pin (I've never seen these built-in but only on
      PCI cards (sometimes two on one card) in a wide range of boxes)

(See one of my previous posts on this topic for common names of these 
connectors and links to pictures.)

That makes 10 combinations altogether.  What I don't have at all is the 
AD combination.  Does such a beast exist?  A few of those I could use.

Of the other combinations, I have enough of some of them.  I need some 
more cables for some of the combinations, though, namely AC, BC, BD, CD 
and DD.  (In other words, the only type I need with the same connectors 
on each end is DD and of those with different connectors on each end, I 
need all except AB (I've never seen AD so I don't know if it exists.)



