Philip, you seem to be on the other side of the pond.

I have a large collection of unused SCSI cables collected over the 
years.  I don't think that an A-D cable was ever manufactured, because 
the fat 50-pin Centronics SCSI is from the earliest epoch of SCSI.  The 
small 68-pin is much newer, and was not used as widely as the "Type C" 
connector.

The 50-pin Centronics and also showed up in the IBM PC and Mac worlds, 
supported by host bus adapter manufacturers like Adaptec, BusLogic, and NCR.

But I can go through my collection and tell you what I have available if 
you are willing to pay for pretty expensive international shipping plus 
a few dollars per cable... Ben Myers


